cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "QEM Auditor"
message: >-
  If you use this software in work you publish, please cite it.
  If it changed a claim you were about to make, that is worth
  saying in the text rather than only in the bibliography.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Venkat
    family-names: Allu
    email: alluvenkat11@gmail.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/Venkatallu11/qem-auditor"
abstract: >-
  An auditor for quantum error-mitigation claims. It does not
  produce a better-corrected number; it designs experiments that
  would destroy a claim, runs them, and reports what survived.
  Fifteen mitigation methods, adversarial controls including a
  deliberate fraud that wins every accuracy leaderboard and is
  caught anyway, an eight-verdict lattice in which an unrun hard
  gate is never a pass, and readers for real hardware job records.
keywords:
  - quantum computing
  - quantum error mitigation
  - reproducibility
  - benchmarking
  - Qiskit
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-27"
